// Zed keymap
//
// Two Linux defaults collide with plain pasting:
//
//   * vim mode binds ctrl-v to vim::PushLiteral in insert mode (Vim's "insert
//     the next character literally") and to vim::ToggleVisualBlock in normal
//     mode, so ctrl-v never pasted;
//   * the Markdown keymap binds ctrl-shift-v to markdown::OpenPreview
//     (assets/keymaps/default-linux.json, context "Editor && extension == md"),
//     so the usual fallback opened the preview instead of pasting.
//
// ctrl-v pastes in every editor context below; visual block stays available on
// ctrl-q, which the vim keymap already binds to vim::ToggleVisualBlock, and the
// Markdown preview stays on ctrl-k v (markdown::OpenPreviewToTheSide).
[
  {
    "context": "Editor",
    "bindings": {
      "ctrl-v": "editor::Paste"
    }
  },
  {
    "context": "Editor && extension == md",
    "bindings": {
      "ctrl-shift-v": "editor::Paste"
    }
  }
]
